WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.870
Episode 22: Four on a Deserted Island

2
00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:08.718
When the flotilla of flower boats clearing Seven
Bridges Haven reached the threshold of the Siren Strait.

3
00:00:08.818 --> 00:00:11.840
The solitary maritime gateway into the continental capital—chilled
tension solidified across the water like winter ice.

4
00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:14.821
Atop the jagged cliffs flanking the narrowest
defile of the strait, three colossal

5
00:00:14.921 --> 00:00:17.810
mana-ballista batteries erected by Lucian's
imperial navy gleamed with lethal menace.

6
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:20.746
While anchored directly in the
mid-channel sat two titanic

7
00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:23.780
black-iron ironclads, enforcing
an airtight maritime blockade.

8
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.411
The siege engines possessed an
effective range of a thousand paces,

9
00:00:26.511 --> 00:00:29.750
rendering any frontal assault by the frail
wooden flower boats an act of suicidal folly.

10
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:32.713
Gripping the helm, Rondol studied
the imperial fortifications

11
00:00:32.813 --> 00:00:35.720
through his brass telescope,
clicking his tongue in frustration.

12
00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:38.847
[Rondol] "Those ironclads draw too much water for our craft
to board them, and their battery arcs overlap completely.

13
00:00:38.947 --> 00:00:41.690
Unless those cliffside ballista towers are silenced first,
not a single flower barge will slip through alive."

14
00:00:41.890 --> 00:00:44.642
Standing upon the timber prow, Kadan
pointed his unadorned iron shield

15
00:00:44.742 --> 00:00:47.660
toward a solitary, wind-scoured reef
rising outside the channel—Gull Crag.

16
00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:53.630
[Kadan] "That rocky islet lies
in the battery blind spot.

17
00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.435
[Celia] If we establish a
beachhead upon those cliffs,

18
00:00:56.535 --> 00:00:59.600
we can construct a counter-siege
weapon to break the blockade."

19
00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:02.635
[Ignis] Cilia swept her Jade Staff, reading the coastal
squalls with a nod of approval. "Violent undertows around Gull

20
00:01:02.735 --> 00:01:05.570
Crag deter imperial patrol cutters from venturing near. We
can establish an encampment there under total concealment."

21
00:01:05.770 --> 00:01:11.540
Ignis clenched his fists, examining the
enemy ships with tactical precision.

22
00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:14.017
"Imperial ironclads boast
impenetrable belt armor,

23
00:01:14.117 --> 00:01:17.510
but their top decking is notoriously
vulnerable to plunging kinetic fire.

24
00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:23.480
[Kadan] If we strike them from the heights,
we can cave in their boiler rooms."

25
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:26.022
Altering their trim under
the cover of sea mist,

26
00:01:26.122 --> 00:01:29.450
the companions dropped anchor upon
the gravel sandbar of Gull Crag.

27
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.858
Though an arid, forbidding rock shelf battered by howling
surf, the shoreline was littered with colossal oak timbers,

28
00:01:32.958 --> 00:01:35.420
shattered keels, and heaps of massive bull kelp
washed ashore from centuries of shipwrecks.

29
00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.643
Slamming his massive double-bitted
battleaxe into the sand,

30
00:01:38.743 --> 00:01:41.390
Grimli the dwarven smith
burst into a roaring laugh.

31
00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:47.360
[Grimli] "Bwahaha!

32
00:01:47.560 --> 00:01:53.330
[Grimli] The sea gods have delivered the
finest siege timber right to our doorsteps!

33
00:01:53.530 --> 00:01:59.300
Look at these seasoned oak
ribs and dense ironwood spars!

34
00:01:59.500 --> 00:02:01.998
[Kadan] Give this old dwarf
half a day, and I shall erect a

35
00:02:02.098 --> 00:02:05.270
triple-torsion counterweight catapult
capable of cracking a citadel wall!"

36
00:02:05.470 --> 00:02:08.271
Drawing his silver dagger to strip the briny

37
00:02:08.371 --> 00:02:11.240
bark from the timbers,
Kadan joined the work.

38
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.665
[Ignis] "Lead the way, Master Grimli.

39
00:02:13.765 --> 00:02:17.210
I will shape the mortises and
drive the locking wedges."

40
00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.536
Ignis gathered granite stones
to construct a makeshift forge,

41
00:02:19.636 --> 00:02:23.180
kindling his immaculate white flame to smelt
discarded anchor chains into heavy iron axle bearings.

42
00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.874
"I will fuse these iron links
into balanced rotating spindles.

43
00:02:25.974 --> 00:02:29.150
We will give those imperial tin cans an
iron greeting they will never forget."

44
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:32.418
Weaving the thick, fibrous bull kelp
into high-tensile torsion cords,

45
00:02:32.518 --> 00:02:35.120
Cilia infused the fibers with
elasticity through wind mana.

46
00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:38.617
[Grimli] Under the unified labor of the
three youths and the master dwarven smith,

47
00:02:38.717 --> 00:02:41.090
the colossal siege engine rapidly
took form upon the cliffs.

48
00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.164
By the time the crimson sun dipped toward
the waves, a magnificent thirty-foot

49
00:02:44.264 --> 00:02:47.060
counterweight catapult stood poised upon
the highest precipice of Gull Crag.

50
00:02:47.260 --> 00:02:49.946
Massive basalt boulders were quarried
as ammunition, upon which Cilia carved

51
00:02:50.046 --> 00:02:53.030
frost runes designed to shatter into concussive
shards of razor ice upon detonation.

52
00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:59.000
Checking the ratchet gears of the winch,
Grimli clapped Kadan's broad shoulder.

53
00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:01.889
[Grimli] "Kadan, lad, your master
Aleksandar and I built just such a

54
00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:04.970
siege thrower amidst the blizzards of
the First Crusade twenty winters ago.

55
00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:07.964
[Grimli] That stubborn knight not only wielded a shield
like a mountain, but he also had the finest hands for

56
00:03:08.064 --> 00:03:10.940
timber and stonework I ever saw. Watching your hammer work
today, I know his craft lives proudly in your blood."

57
00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:12.990
Resting against his shield,

58
00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:16.910
Kadan gazed across the sunset
swells with a serene smile.

59
00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.957
[Kadan] "Master Aleksandar taught me that craft is never about
senseless destruction, but the manifestation of wisdom to

60
00:03:20.057 --> 00:03:22.880
protect the vulnerable. This catapult is not a weapon of
slaughter, but the key to open a path of life for our people."

61
00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:28.850
Coating the throwing basket with sanctifying
fire, Ignis spoke in quiet reverence.

62
00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.042
[Ignis] "The road once
walked by father Balian and

63
00:03:32.142 --> 00:03:34.820
uncle Aleksandar... is
now ours to complete."

64
00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:37.906
Just then, alarm klaxons blared across the
strait as two swift imperial scouting pinnaces

65
00:03:38.006 --> 00:03:40.790
detected the activity upon the crag, surging
forward with archers nocking fire arrows.

66
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.114
[Celia] Sweeping her Jade Staff,

67
00:03:43.214 --> 00:03:46.760
Cilia conjured dense oceanic
fog around the heights.

68
00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:52.730
"I will shroud the peak in
mist to blind their bowmen!

69
00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:58.700
[Celia] Stand ready!"

70
00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.515
As milky-white fog swallowed the rock shelf,

71
00:04:01.615 --> 00:04:04.670
Kadan gripped the release
lever with steady nerves.

72
00:04:04.870 --> 00:04:07.203
[Grimli] "Target: imperial
flagship engine bay,

73
00:04:07.303 --> 00:04:10.640
three thousand paces ahead!" Grimli
hammered down the locking dog.

74
00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:16.610
[Grimli] "Loose the stone, lad!"

75
00:04:16.810 --> 00:04:22.580
Boom!

76
00:04:22.780 --> 00:04:25.973
With a concussive crack of bending timber,
the catapult arm cleaved through the air,

77
00:04:26.073 --> 00:04:28.550
hurling the frost-inscribed basalt
monolith into the twilight sky.

78
00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:31.831
Like a roaring meteor, the projectile arced over the channel, crashing
dead-center through the armored deck of the lead imperial ironclad.

79
00:04:31.931 --> 00:04:34.520
Crr-aaash! The thick iron plate buckled like parchment as
the frost runes detonated in an apocalyptic freezing blast.

80
00:04:34.720 --> 00:04:37.238
The arcane steam boilers ruptured
in cascading detonations,

81
00:04:37.338 --> 00:04:40.490
vomiting black smoke as the flagship
tilted violently onto its beam ends.

82
00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.443
In rapid succession, the second and third projectiles
slammed squarely into the cliffside ballista towers.

83
00:04:43.543 --> 00:04:46.460
Hundreds of tons of pulverized granite cascaded into the
sea, burying the imperial artillery beneath landslides.

84
00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:49.634
With the ironclads crippled
and the gun towers silenced,

85
00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:52.430
the passage through the
Siren Strait lay wide open.

86
00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:55.736
From the hundreds of flower boats holding position
offshore erupted a deafening roar of triumph.

87
00:04:55.836 --> 00:04:58.400
Hoisting his sails, Rondol sounded the
conch horn to signal the general advance.

88
00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:01.241
Standing beside the timber catapult,
Kadan, Ignis, and Cilia watched the

89
00:05:01.341 --> 00:05:04.370
refugee flotilla glide safely through the
gap, letting out long breaths of relief.

90
00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:08.238
Passing a leather flask of
potent dwarven ale to Kadan,

91
00:05:08.338 --> 00:05:10.340
Grimli barked a hearty chuckle.

92
00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:16.310
[Grimli] "Magnificently done, children!
The first iron gate is shattered!

93
00:05:16.510 --> 00:05:19.008
[Kadan] Now let us march to
the secret grottos of Mount

94
00:05:19.108 --> 00:05:22.280
Dragonhorn and reclaim the ancestral
heritage left by our forebears!"

95
00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:28.250
Taking a deep draught, Kadan nodded firmly.

96
00:05:28.450 --> 00:05:34.220
"Forward, companions.

97
00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:37.128
[Kadan] The dawn of the continent is at
hand." Leaving Gull Crag in their wake,

98
00:05:37.228 --> 00:05:40.190
the companions resumed their resolute voyage
toward the foothills of Mount Dragonhorn.

99
00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:46.160
